# Copy to .env (gitignored). Compose loads it from the repo root when you run `pnpm dev`.

# REQUIRED — master key for the per-user Anthropic token vault (data/secrets/).
# Each signed-in user stores their own token via Settings; it is encrypted with
# this key (AES-256-GCM). Without it the app refuses to accept or use tokens.
# Generate once:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
SECRETS_MASTER_KEY=

# DEV-ONLY fallback: let tasks whose owner has no stored token fall back to the
# shared credentials below (or the ambient ~/.claude login). Off by default so
# users can never silently run on someone else's identity. Set to 1 to enable.
# ALLOW_SHARED_TOKEN_FALLBACK=

# Shared Claude credentials — ONLY used when ALLOW_SHARED_TOKEN_FALLBACK=1.
# Normal setup: each user saves their own token in Settings instead (generate a
# subscription token with `claude setup-token`, or paste an API key).
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Folders the "Browse…" folder picker may list when adding a project (colon-separated,
# PATH-style; the FIRST entry is where it opens). Compose already sets HOST paths
# (~/:/Users:/Volumes), so you only need it here to narrow the picker, or to add a path
# outside those — which also needs a matching bind mount in compose, or the folder just
# lists empty. `/` browses everything the container can see, container internals included.
# Typing/pasting a path into the Add-project field is not restricted by this.
# PROJECT_ROOTS=/Users/you/Dev:/Volumes/SSD/src

# GitHub auth for the container — lets agents run `gh pr create` and the UI push/pull
# over HTTPS. macOS keychain/SSH creds don't cross into Linux, so the container needs
# its own token. Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens with `repo` scope
# (classic), or a fine-grained token with Contents + Pull requests read/write.
# gh and git both pick this up automatically (no `gh auth login` needed).
# GH_TOKEN=
